According to 3GPP TS 24.501, when releasing a PDU session due to errors in QoS operations or packet filters, the UE shall include a "PDU Session Release Request" message with an "Cause" set to "reactivation of a PDU session due to a QoS operation" or "semantic error in the QoS operation" or "syntactic error in the QoS operation" or "an error in the packet filter" as the cause value.

More specifically, the UE shall include the cause value in the PDU SESSION RELEASE REQUEST message as follows:

- The UE sets the "Cause" value to:
  - #29 "reactivation of a PDU session due to a QoS operation";
  - #32 "semantic error in the QoS operation";
  - #33 "syntactic error in the QoS operation";
  - #34 "an error in the packet filter".

This is as per clause 5.2.2.3 of 3GPP TS 24.501.

According to 3GPP TS 24.501, subclause 5.6.1.2:

The UE shall:

> perform a NAS security configuration as specified in subclause 5.4.2 if the SERVICE ACCEPT message includes a NAS security configuration;

> configure the NAS signalling connection as specified in subclause 5.7;

> enter state EMM-REGISTERED.NORMAL if the UE was in state EMM-DEREGISTERED or EMM-REGISTERED.ATTEMPTING-TO-REGISTER or EMM-REGISTERED.RELEASE-SUSPENDED or EMM-REGISTERED.DEREGISTERED and the SERVICE ACCEPT message was received on a NAS signalling connection that was successfully established;

> enter state EMM-REGISTERED.NORMAL if the UE was in state EMM-REGISTERED.INACTIVE and the SERVICE ACCEPT message was received on the same NAS signalling connection that was previously successfully established;

> consider the NAS sequence number of the received SERVICE ACCEPT message as the reference for the NAS sequence number synchronization;

> update its NAS sequence number for the given NAS signalling connection as specified in subclause 5.4.1;

> reset the timer T3517 and stop re-transmitting the SERVICE REQUEST message if it was running;

> send a SERVICE COMPLETE message to the network if the UE has a NAS signalling connection successfully established;

> discard any pending NAS uplink data that was waiting to be sent.
